{"seq": 49, "time": "2026-11-17T12:59:54.130Z", "kind": "note", "data": {"batch": "loop-1", "change": "Three fixes to the loop's plumbing; the acceptance rule, panel, T = 3, caps, stop rules and move kinds are unchanged. (1) The proposer never ran on Modal: it was told to read lab/prompts from this checkout, which a Modal sandbox does not hold, so m01 and m02 came from the rules fallback. It now reads copies of the editable prompts in its own workspace. (2) The loop crashed during m02's evaluation on a past.dev network error (5 tries, about 15 s of backoff); past.dev calls now retry 8 times with about 2 minutes of backoff. (3) A crashed loop can now resume from its ledger entries (--resume-loop): moves made, rejections in a row and the incumbent are rebuilt, the move being judged is judged again in its own run folder, and spend so far is read back from the event logs so the $400 cap still covers the whole loop. The four failed proposer attempts are counted at their $1.50 estimates each though they spent nothing.", "what": "deviation during loop-1 (after m01 was judged, before m02 was evaluated)"}, "prev_sha": "00c248ca7a8f932d1d935e1d2897681afdafe4395f935c82eff47f5f2808c684", "sha": "d1e37db3b40c0068c82e5c3c3f4b7b0e0914e34e343d91ced6bab69bb7c42267"}
